# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAFE -- repository hygiene
#
# Only source, scripts, parsed results, and the trace manifest belong in git.
# Build output and simulator dumps are regenerable: build_variants.sh + probe.sh.
#
# The malloc/free-instrumented traces (trace/*.xz, ~2.8 GB) ship as GitHub
# *Release assets*, not git objects -- 18 of the 25 exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard
# per-file limit. Fetch them with fetch_traces.sh; trace/SHA256SUMS pins them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
*.o
*.so
*.a
tracer/obj-intel64/

# Stray built binaries committed by accident
/ip_guard

# --- Simulator output / results dumps --------------------------------------
# Regenerable: re-run build_variants.sh + probe.sh / run.sh.
# The parsed summary (Results_IPC.csv) IS tracked.
probe_output/
temp_output/
sanity/
/output/

# Per-benchmark debug dumps (GB-scale plaintext dumps of execution)
/debug.txt
/temp.txt
/pop2.txt
/roms523.txt
/gcc_s-734.txt

# --- Logs / scratch --------------------------------------------------------
*.log
/master_log.txt

# --- Traces -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Instrumented traces come from Release assets (see fetch_traces.sh). The
# SHA256SUMS manifest in that directory IS tracked, so it must not be ignored.
/trace/*.xz
/trace/*.trace
/trace/*.trace.txt

# --- Editor / OS / Python --------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.*.sw?
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*~
.DS_Store
